From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 19:30:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] qasf: Decommit allocators before stopping the asynchronous
 reader.

The WM reader can deliver one final sample while the filter graph is being
stopped. If the downstream allocator has no available sample, that delivery
blocks in IMemAllocator::GetBuffer(). The same WM reader callback thread is
responsible for processing the queued stop operation and sending WMT_STOPPED,
so waiting for WMT_STOPPED before decommitting the allocator deadlocks.

Decommit connected output allocators first. This wakes blocked GetBuffer()
calls and prevents new samples from being acquired, allowing the callback
thread to finish delivery and process the stop operation.
---
 dlls/qasf/asfreader.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/qasf/asfreader.c b/dlls/qasf/asfreader.c
index 2cc4d68..edcd908 100644
--- a/dlls/qasf/asfreader.c
+++ b/dlls/qasf/asfreader.c
@@ -617,9 +617,6 @@ static HRESULT asf_reader_cleanup_stream(struct strmbase_filter *iface)
 
     TRACE("iface %p\n", iface);
 
-    if (FAILED(hr = asf_reader_stop_stream(filter)))
-        WARN("Failed to stop WMReader %p, hr %#lx\n", filter->reader, hr);
-
     for (i = 0; i < filter->stream_count; ++i)
     {
         struct asf_stream *stream = filter->streams + i;
@@ -634,6 +631,9 @@ static HRESULT asf_reader_cleanup_stream(struct strmbase_filter *iface)
         }
     }
 
+    if (FAILED(hr = asf_reader_stop_stream(filter)))
+        WARN("Failed to stop WMReader %p, hr %#lx\n", filter->reader, hr);
+
     return hr;
 }
 
